<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Simplifying combined multiplication and division of surds into the form k√m</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Simplify the following expression, giving your answer in the form \(k\sqrt{m}\), where \(m\) has no perfect-square factors. <i>(Note: For example, write <code>3*sqrt(5)</code> to represent \(3\sqrt{5}\).)</i></p>
<p style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em;">\[ \frac{{@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}} \times {@b@}\sqrt{{@m@}}}{{@c@}\sqrt{{@m@}}} \]</p>
<p>Simplified form = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Step 1: Multiply the numerator</b><br>
Multiply the numbers outside the square roots, then multiply the numbers inside the square roots:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@a@} \times {@b@} = {@ab@}, \qquad \sqrt{{@n@}} \times \sqrt{{@m@}} = \sqrt{{@n@} \times {@m@}} = \sqrt{{@nm@}}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}} \times {@b@}\sqrt{{@m@}} = {@ab@}\sqrt{{@nm@}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 2: Rewrite the fraction and divide the outside numbers</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@ab@}\sqrt{{@nm@}}}{{@c@}\sqrt{{@m@}}} \quad \Longrightarrow \quad {@ab@} \div {@c@} = {@e@}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 3: Divide the square roots using \(\dfrac{\sqrt{x}}{\sqrt{y}} = \sqrt{\dfrac{x}{y}}\)</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{\sqrt{{@nm@}}}{\sqrt{{@m@}}} = \sqrt{\frac{{@nm@}}{{@m@}}} = \sqrt{{@n@}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 4: Combine the results</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}} \times {@b@}\sqrt{{@m@}}}{{@c@}\sqrt{{@m@}}} = {@e@} \times \sqrt{{@n@}} = {@ta1@}\)</p>

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \frac{{@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}} \times {@b@}\sqrt{{@m@}}}{{@c@}\sqrt{{@m@}}} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
